>  * How safe is it to jump in the hole? Will it ever land me in the water

I've jumped through holes thousands of times and never landed in water, 
so (without checking the source) I'll say you won't land in water.  But 
if you were exceptionally unfortunate you might land on one of the tiny 
islands.  Got a /Cold?

>  * How should I go about getting a cursed potion of gain level? I have a 
>    bunch of gain level, actually, but I don't think any are cursed, and I 
>    converted my only non-coaligned altar. Are there tricks to curse things
>    I haven't thought of?

Dipping an item (such as a potion of water) in a fountain has a 1/30 
chance of cursing it.  And once you have one, you can easily make as many 
as you need. Worth a shot, if you have any fountains remaining.  You 
could also a try a confused reading of a ?oRC; see the scroll spoiler for 
details.  But I wouldn't waste c!oGL on this quest.   

>  * Should I bless all my identify scrolls, collect all the rings around
>    and try to find polycontrol, and then just poly into a xorn both ways?
>    I've got wands of polymorph all over the place.

A nice long polypile session looks like your best next step.  You will 
hopefully also obtain =Conflict (extremely important), =Levitation, and 
=FreeAction.  You should also polypile potions (alchemy), scrolls (but 
save enough blank ones), spellbooks (obvious), magic armor (maybe you'll 
get a helm of brilliance), magic tools (hoping for magic marker), wands 
(hoping for /digging and /teleport and maybe a couple /death).  Google 
groups archive has extensive discussion of proper polypiling teqchnique, 
if you need it.  

